  "proposition": "During real hand movement, absolute sensorimotor (C3/C4) mu (8-13 Hz) and beta (13-30 Hz) power drops relative to rest -- event-related desynchronization, the signal a motor BCI decodes -- in 5 of 5 eegmmidb subjects for mu (mean -15.2%) and 5/5 for beta, reproduced from 10 frozen substrate runs with every band-power claim of the primary (S001 rest) GROUNDED and a byte-identical replay. Contralateral lateralization is present but noisy per subject and is not claimed; the reported, robust quantity is the desynchronization itself.",
